Falsifies `machine_statistics_contract::verification::the_reader_admits_exactly_the_pages_it_names`.

The defect: the magic compare looks at the low 32 bits of the word only, so a page whose magic
differs in its upper half is admitted. Every host test flips the lowest bit of the magic, which
the shortened compare still catches, so the defect is invisible to them.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(admitted)` in the arm that returned a page, on a page whose upper magic bytes differ.

